{
  "name": "tawny owl",
  "kind": "parts",
  "_about": "a tawny owl: plump, the big round head over an egg-shaped body, NO ear tufts; warm brown above mottled darker with a row of pale scapular spots, buff below with dark shaft streaks and fine bars; the facial disc of two lobes, one round each eye, meeting over the bill, rimmed by a thin dark line, the pale brows rising in a V from the bill; big dark eyes set into the disc in blue-grey lids; the small pale hooked bill half buried; the legs and toes feathered buff, dark talons",
